  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream is a traditional Italian dessert made with three flavors: chocolate, strawberry, and vanilla. It's sometimes referred to as \"Trio\" in some regions. Here's a simple and authentic recipe you can follow at home:\n\n---\n\n### **Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream (Trio) Recipe**\n\n#### **Ingredients** (for 4\u20136 servings):\n\n- 2 cups heavy cream (35% or higher)\n- 1 cup whole milk\n- 1/2 cup sugar\n- 1/2 cup chocolate sauce or melted dark chocolate (60% cacao or higher)\n- 1/2 cup strawberry puree or mashed strawberries (fresh or frozen)\n- 1/2 cup vanilla ice cream mix or 1/2 cup vanilla ice cream (store-bought or homemade)\n- 1/2 cup traditional Neapolitan ice cream mix (optional, for authentic texture, or skip if using store-bought)\n- Optional: 1/4 tsp vanilla extract\n\n---\n\n### **Instructions**:\n\n1. **Churn the Base**:\n   - In a large mixing bowl, combine the heavy cream, whole milk, and sugar.\n   - Whisk until the sugar is fully dissolved.\n   - Churn this mixture in an ice cream maker according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions, usually for about 20\u201325 minutes, until it reaches a soft-serve consistency.\n\n2. **Add the Flavors**:\n   - Once the base is ready, divide it into three equal portions in separate bowls or containers.\n   - **Chocolate Portion**: Stir in 1/2 cup melted chocolate sauce or dark chocolate until fully mixed.\n   - **Strawberry Portion**: Stir in 1/2 cup strawberry puree or mashed strawberries.\n   - **Vanilla Portion**: Add 1/2 cup vanilla ice cream mix or use a store-bought vanilla ice cream for the third portion.\n\n3. **Freeze**:\n   - Cover each portion separately and freeze for at least 2 hours, or until firm. You can also swirl the flavors together before freezing for a marbled effect.\n\n4. **Scoop and Serve**:\n   - When ready to serve, scoop each flavor into separate bowls or cones, or mix them together for a classic \"Neapolitan\" blend.\n   - Serve immediately, or briefly soften in the refrigerator before serving.\n\n---\n\n### **Notes**:\n- For an even more authentic experience, you can make each flavor separately and then mix them together in a bowl before freezing.\n- Traditional Neapolitan ice cream is often made with a base of egg yolks and sugar, then whipped into a meringue-like texture before freezing. This version simplifies the process using an ice cream maker.\n- If you don\u2019t have an ice cream maker, you can churn the mixture in a large container in the freezer, stirring every 30 minutes for 2\u20133 hours until it thickens.\n\nLet me know if you\u2019d like a version that uses store-bought mixes or a no-churn recipe!",
